# Everything captured off the running machine is encrypted at rest with
# git-crypt. The working tree stays plaintext, so capture-system.sh and the
# installer are unaffected; only what git stores is ciphertext.
#
# This covers the whole system/ tree, not just system/generated/. The /etc
# files identify the machine just as clearly: smb.conf alone carries the
# hostname, the username, the wireless interface and the LAN allow-list.
#
# See docs/SECRETS.md before cloning or pushing this.
system/** filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt
